5. YOUR DATA AND THIRD-PARTY SERVICES

  (a) Votes, favorites, lists, history, and settings you create are stored in
      your own browser. If you choose to share votes for the Hall of Fame,
      those votes and your GitHub username are published in a GitHub issue
      and counted in the public leaderboard. Sharing is optional.

  (b) The Software has no account system, no analytics, and no telemetry.

  (c) The Software is hosted on GitHub Pages and its robot runs on GitHub
      Actions. Website previews are loaded from WordPress mShots and archive
      years from the Internet Archive. Those services' own privacy terms apply
      to requests made to them.

  (d) Links in the Software lead to third-party websites. Cambric does not
      own, control, or endorse those websites or their content.

6. DISCOVERY RESULTS

The Software reports what its automated checks observe; it does not guarantee
an outcome. A website marked as working was reachable when last checked, not
necessarily now. Categories, names, and descriptions are chosen automatically
and may be wrong. A passed safety check means no warning sign was found, not
that a website is safe. Use your own judgement before visiting or trusting any
website.

